const teachingByDepth={FOUNDATIONAL_CONCEPT:['Confusing productivity or price with the relevant opportunity-cost rule.','Comparative advantage is determined by relative opportunity cost.'],ABSOLUTE_VS_COMPARATIVE:['Using greater output alone to assign comparative advantage.','Absolute advantage concerns productivity; comparative advantage concerns lower opportunity cost.'],SIMPLE_OPPORTUNITY_COST:['Computing or comparing the opportunity costs in the wrong direction.','Compute the forgone alternative per unit, then select the lower opportunity cost.'],RECIPROCAL_OPPORTUNITY_COST:['Repeating a ratio instead of taking its reciprocal.','Reverse both the goods and the ratio when changing opportunity-cost orientation.'],SPECIALIZATION:['Assigning every activity to the absolutely more productive producer.','In the textbook model, specialization follows comparative advantage.'],TERMS_OF_TRADE:['Including a boundary or a rate outside the two opportunity costs as a strict mutual gain.','A strict mutual-gain rate lies strictly between the relevant opportunity costs.'],CONCEPTUAL_GAINS:['Assuming higher combined output makes every possible exchange mutually beneficial.','Specialization creates potential output gains; the trading terms determine whether both sides gain.'],NUMERICAL_GAIN_ONE_PARTY:['Comparing a post-trade bundle with specialization output instead of the stated autarky bundle.','Subtract the stated autarky bundle from post-trade consumption good by good.'],NUMERICAL_GAIN_BOTH_PARTIES:['Using the wrong autarky bundle or failing to conserve the traded goods.','Derive both post-trade bundles and compare each with its stated autarky bundle.'],FULL_TRADE_MODEL:['Skipping a required link among opportunity cost, specialization, exchange, and the autarky comparison.','Work through the complete model in order and keep the ratio units fixed.'],DISTRIBUTION_OF_GAINS:['Equating positive aggregate gains with equal or universal individual gains.','Total gains and their distribution are distinct; terms of trade allocate the modeled surplus.'],DYNAMIC_TRANSFER:['Treating comparative advantage as fixed after productivity or opportunity costs change.','Recompute relative opportunity costs after a change and respect the model limits.']};
